Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional continuous $K$-representation of a local Galois group or of $G_{F,S}$. Continuous cohomology is finite dimensional and satisfies local duality, local and global Euler characteristics, and Poitou–Tate duality with arbitrary linear local conditions. The twist in characteristic two is the residual Tate twist. At real places local duality uses Tate cohomology; the $h^0_v$ appearing in the Euler and Selmer formulas below still denotes the dimension of ordinary invariants. In particular, if $F$ is totally real of degree $d$ and $\dim_KV=r$, then $$\begin{aligned}
h^0_v(V)-h^1_v(V)+h^2_v(V)&=-r[F_v:\mathbb Q_2]
                       &&(v\mid2),\\
h^0(V)-h^1(V)+h^2(V)&=-rd+\sum_{v\mid\infty}h^0_v(V).
\label{eq:global-euler-curve}
\end{aligned}$$ At a real place the local contribution to a Selmer dimension difference is $\dim L_v-h^0_v(V)$, where $L_v\subset H^1(F_v,V)$. The same formulas, with the usual real-place interpretation, hold for finite $2$-adic coefficient fields.

Let $F$ be totally real of degree $d$, let $S$ contain the real and dyadic places, and let $\rho$ be a representation over a finite residue field, a curve field as above, or a finite $2$-adic field. Use one global frame and a fixed determinant. Let $T\subset S$ consist of all real places and $m$ dyadic places, each isomorphic to $\mathbb Q_2$. Over the completed product of the unrestricted local framed deformation rings at $T$, the global framed ring has a power-series presentation with $g$ relative variables and $r$ relations satisfying $$\label{eq:relative-one-frame}
g-r\ge 3-6m-h^0\bigl(D^\vee(1)\bigr).$$ Local quotient conditions and local line charts may then be imposed by base change without changing this bound. This includes replacing the local base by its reduction.*


*For the variable-determinant problem with independent frames at the places of $S$, the relative tangent dimension over the local framed base is $$\label{eq:relative-independent-frames}
h^1_{\mathrm{Sel}}(\mathop{\mathrm{ad}}\rho)
 +\sum_{v\in S}h^0_v(\mathop{\mathrm{ad}}\rho)-h^0(\mathop{\mathrm{ad}}\rho),$$ where the Selmer condition is zero at $S$ and any other prescribed conditions are included in the Selmer group. On the absolutely irreducible locus, forgetting these independent frames has smooth fiber dimension $4|S|-1$.

On $N_{\eta,\infty}$ the sequence $\varpi,V_1,\ldots,V_h$ is regular. Moreover $$\begin{aligned}
 \dim\mathop{\mathrm{Supp}}_{R_{\eta,\infty}}N_{\eta,\infty}
       &\geq2d+4s+h,                                  \label{eq:patched-dimension}\\
 N_{\eta,\infty}/(V_1,\ldots,V_h)N_{\eta,\infty}
       &\simeq (N_\eta^{\oplus2^h})^*.                \label{eq:patched-augmentation}
\end{aligned}$$
